Description:A tool that makes the X-12-ARIMA PICKMDL procedure available within the JDemetra+ R Framework (<https://github.com/rjdverse).
             PICKMDL is a model selection procedure that differs from the automdl procedure implemented in JDemetra+. The pickmdl procedure restricts 
             the choice of seasonal ARIMA models to an ordered set of parsimonious models, the first sARIMA model that fulfills a predefined set of 
             three criteria is selected. This restriction may lead to more stable model selection and thus less future revisions. A limitation of the procedure, however,
             is that an inadequate sARIMA model may be selected if none of the models on the list fits the data well. To mitigate this risk, the pickdml3 
             package provides the option to fall back on the automdl procedure. The pickmdl3 package further includes functionality to support an orderly production 
             process when using the X-13 methodology in rjd3. The package provides functionality that facilitates the process of partial concurrent adjustment, 
             i.e. yearly model and outlier selection. The package also includes functions for seasonal adjustment of multiple series based 
             on a data frame with model specifications, as well as a graphical user interface for creating, editing, and saving such data frames. 
